### 5. Avoid logging secrets

If you add configuration logging, avoid logging raw environment variables.

Bad:

```js
console.log(process.env);
```

Bad:

```js
console.log('Database URL:', process.env.DATABASE_URL);
```

Safer:

```js
console.log('Database configured:', Boolean(process.env.DATABASE_URL));
```

Or redact:

```js
function redact(value) {
  if (!value) return undefined;
  return `${value.slice(0, 4)}...redacted`;
}

console.log('API token configured:', Boolean(process.env.API_TOKEN));
```

