## 2. Missing authorization

### Issue

Authentication answers “who are you?” Authorization answers “are you allowed to do this?”

Even if authentication is added, `/users` should not automatically be available to every authenticated user. User listing endpoints are often administrative.

### Recommendation

Add role- or permission-based authorization.

Example:

```js
function requireRole(role) {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    if (!req.user || !Array.isArray(req.user.roles)) {
      return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' });
    }

    if (!req.user.roles.includes(role)) {
      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
    }

    next();
  };
}

app.get('/users', authenticateUser, requireRole('admin'), (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob' },
  ]);
});
```

