## 12. Hardcoded port

### Severity: Low

The server always listens on port `3000`.

```js
app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});
```

This is not directly a security vulnerability, but it is a deployment concern. In production, the port should typically come from environment configuration.

### Recommendation

```js
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

app.listen(PORT, () => {
