# Findings

## 1. `/users` exposes user data without authentication

### Severity: High if this endpoint represents real users

The `/users` route returns user records, including email addresses, to anyone who can access the server.

```js
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});
